 "originals_policy": "Unredacted originals are available to the editor and reviewers on request; they contain internal server addresses and are not published.",
 "release_changes": "Code-release copy of the bundle manifest: the internal store identifiers of each file were removed; paths of the result files that cite a recorded hash were changed to their location under results/; references to duplicate copies of rule files that exist in the manuscript bundle but not in this repository (a second copy of tois_v7_rule.json, fh_decision_rule.json, c4_protocol.json and of the four v7.6 rule files) were removed. The rule files themselves were byte-identical to the manuscript bundle up to release v3 (see the release v4 note on host numbers below). Release v3 (2026-10-16) adds the five v7.8 registration files (framing rule, amendment 1 and its registered serialisation, external-comparator protocol notes 1 and 2), redacted with the same rules; they were registered after the manuscript bundle was built and are marked added_in. The two protocol notes are time-stamped in created_utc (manifest key time_field). Release v4 (2026-10-17) adds the seven v7.9 fresh-window documents (rule, amendment 1, implementation note, addendum 1, freeze manifest, uninspected check, verdict) with content_hash and content_hash_kind; byte-identical copies are also under fresh_window/registration/. Release v4 also lists, under cited_in, the hash fields of the v7.8 and fit-population result files now shipped under results/v78/ and results/fitpop/. Release v4 redaction rules v2 also replace analysis-platform identifiers by neutral text (one field group of fresh_window_uninspected_check.json); their patterns are not published and are read with --originals from platform_rules.json, provided with the originals. Release v4 also redacts bare host numbers that releases 1-3 had left in host-context sentences of four v1-redacted files (hardening_decision_rule.json, a_presub_rule.json, v76_rule.json, v76_rule_registered.json; same changed fields, more <HOST> placeholders, counts in redaction_map.json); the host rules (address-octet labels and bare-host-number contexts) are likewise not published and are read with --originals from label_rules.json, provided with the originals. These four copies therefore differ from the copies in the manuscript bundle, whose recorded hashes (computed from the originals) are unchanged."
}